  abstract = {showed asymmetricalVj-gating properties with respect toVj = 0. Themacroscopic Gj showed substantial reduction (by 82%atVj = 100mV)whendepolarizingCx50expressing cell, whereas a moderate reduction (by 61% at Vj = 100mV) when hyperpolarizing Cx50-expressing cell. This observation is in agreement with previous finding that Cx50 hemichannel gates when the cell is depolarized. Single Cx50/Cx50Cx36N heterotypic channel displayed a main conductance of ~120pS at low Vj pulses (5 20mV), but the conductance rectified with increasing Vj pulses. Cx50/Cx50N9RheterotypicGJ channel also exhibited asymmetricalVjgating properties at macroscopic level, and single channel recordings indicated a main conductance of ~150pS at Vj = 20mV. These results demonstrate that the Vj-gating properties and unitary conductance of Cx50 hemichannels were evidently modified when docking with Cx50-Cx36N or Cx50N9R mutants. These novel properties of heterotypic channels provide insights into the Vj-gating mechanisms of Cx50 GJ channels.},
